# Citation metadata for Bulwark.
#
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo reads it when
# archiving a release — so the DOI it mints carries these authors and this title
# rather than a bare repository slug.
#
# On release: bump `version` and `date-released` to match the git tag, then add the
# minted DOI under `identifiers` (and, once a paper exists, uncomment
# `preferred-citation` so tooling cites the paper while still resolving the software).
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bulwark: a security stack for agentic AI"
message: "If you use this software or its findings in your research, please cite it."
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Mohit
    family-names: Kumar
    email: mkd1112002@gmail.com

repository-code: "https://github.com/mk12002/Bulwark"
url: "https://mk12002.github.io/Bulwark/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-07

abstract: >-
  Bulwark is a defensive security suite for the AI agent supply chain, composed of three
  scanners that audit a system at three levels. Airlock statically analyses the parts —
  ML model artifacts, MCP servers, and tool specifications — for malicious serialization,
  tool poisoning, and provenance gaps. Warden audits the assembly, treating an agent's
  tools, scopes, prompt, and autonomy as a capability graph in order to detect excessive
  agency and toxic tool combinations that no individual component exhibits. Manifest
  inventories the whole system as a standards-based CycloneDX or SPDX AI-BOM with NIST AI
  RMF and EU AI Act control mapping, folding the other two tools' findings in inline.
  The suite is deterministic-first, never executes or imports the artifacts it inspects,
  and expresses its detection logic as YAML rule packs rather than code. It is validated
  at all three levels: a corpus study over public models, an adversarial evasion suite,
  a four-way benchmark against existing pickle scanners, cross-framework invariance and
  false-positive studies for the assembly layer, and discovery-recall and
  standards-conformance studies for the system layer.

keywords:
  - ai-security
  - supply-chain-security
  - static-analysis
  - machine-learning
  - agentic-ai
  - model-context-protocol
  - sbom
  - ai-bom
  - cyclonedx
  - excessive-agency
  - least-privilege
  - ai-governance

# Uncomment and complete once the Zenodo DOI is minted:
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: "Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest release"

# Uncomment once a paper exists, so citations point at the paper:
# preferred-citation:
#   type: article
#   title: "..."
#   authors:
#     - given-names: Mohit
#       family-names: Kumar
#   year: 2026
